{"_id":"696639f43eeddc26d7c3aa0f","roadmapSlug":"ruby","nodeId":"ufLdyKM3iya8zuMD1_sIj","description":"# Metaprogramming\n\nMetaprogramming is essentially writing code that manipulates other code. It allows you to define methods, classes, or even modify existing ones at runtime. This means your program can dynamically adapt and change its behavior based on conditions or data it encounters while running, rather than being fixed at compile time.","resources":[{"type":"book","title":"Metaprogramming Ruby.pdf","url":"https://theswissbay.ch/pdf/Gentoomen%20Library/Programming/Ruby/Metaprogramming%20Ruby.pdf","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd831"},{"type":"article","title":"Ruby Metaprogramming: How to Write Dynamic Code","url":"https://betterstack.com/community/guides/scaling-ruby/metaprogramming/","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd832"},{"type":"article","title":"An Introduction to Metaprogramming in Ruby","url":"https://blog.appsignal.com/2023/07/26/an-introduction-to-metaprogramming-in-ruby.html","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd833"},{"type":"article","title":"Ruby Metaprogramming: Real-World Examples","url":"https://www.rubyguides.com/2016/04/metaprogramming-in-the-wild/","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd834"},{"type":"article","title":"Ruby Metaprogramming Secrets","url":"https://www.rubyguides.com/guides/metaprogramming-guide.pdf","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd835"},{"type":"video","title":"RubyConf 2022: In Defense of Ruby Metaprogramming By Noel Rappin","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D_ZRaZucjm4","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd836"}],"createdAt":"2026-01-13T12:26:28.093Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:06:51.273Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ruby/content/ufLdyKM3iya8zuMD1_sIj.md"}